{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1306245-2e-why-is-the-rate-of-advancement-ludicrously-high-now","id":1306245,"title":"2E - Why is the rate of advancement ludicrously high now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-20T07:21:43-07:00","id":1306245,"title":"2E - Why is the rate of advancement ludicrously high now?","content":"When I first skimmed through the advancement section, I had assumed that they simply made Group Beats the default, which was kind of neat, I guess. But on a closer read today...<br /> That's not what they did. At all.<br /> <br /> Let's look at a group of four players that each earn, on average, five beats per session.<br /> <br /> 1) Under individual beats, they each earn five individual beats, and end the session with 1 Experience.<br /> 2) Under group beats, they contribute to a shared pool consisting of 20 beats, which get distributed evenly amongst them at the end of the session, ending with 1 Experience each<br /> 3) Under this 'Common Pool', they contribute to a shared pool of 20 beats. For every 5 beats in the pool, <i>each character</i> gets 1 experience. They end the session with <b>4 Experiences </b>each.<br /> <br /> ...<i>what?</i><br /> Is this an error or some sort of oversight?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T09:44:53-07:00","id":1306270,"title":"","content":"I believe there's still a cap of one beat per source per scene,